# Private repo: nearly everything is committed, including the dataset splits,
# the raw corpora, and the trained model. Only three kinds of things stay out.

# 1. Secrets. The repo is private, but a leaked key is a leaked key the moment
#    the repo is ever shared, forked, or the account is compromised.
*.env
.env*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
!testdata/**/*.pem

# 2. Things that are platform-specific or regenerable, so committing them would
#    BREAK a clone on another machine or just add churn (not a privacy choice).
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
coverage.out
*.egg-info/
bin/
dist/
.DS_Store
s1-sidecar/s1-sidecar
vendor/crs/.git/

# 3. Local-only accidents from the folder move: a full nested DUPLICATE of the
#    whole project (csf/, ~676 MB, same files again) and the export zips.
/csf/
*.zip

# NOTE: data/ (splits + raw CSIC/ECML corpora) and model/artifacts/ (the trained
# S3 model) are now COMMITTED. Keep this repo PRIVATE -- the corpora are licensed
# datasets whose terms restrict redistribution.
